## So What?

The most important finding of this session is not a site fix — it's the dual-C structural issue surfaced by three independent visitor personas. If C(ρ) and C=f(γ,D,S) are the same observable, a bridge derivation is the most important missing piece in the archive and would vindicate the "one equation" claim. If they're not, the homepage is wrong at the level of its central organizing metaphor. This is the productive kind of wrong: a specific, resolvable question. The TEST-03 kill criterion is also now resolved to "presumptively failed" rather than "ambiguous" — which is the more honest position given the literal reading of the documented numbers.
